cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the cortical bone mapping method
  (Treece et al.), its global/regularised extensions (Neeteson & Boyd 2025),
  both listed under references, and this implementation including the
  version you used.
type: software
title: "cortical-bone-mapping-rs: cortical bone mapping in Rust with Python bindings"
abstract: >-
  Model-based cortical thickness measurement (cortical bone mapping) from
  CT and HR-pQCT images, with local, multigrid and spatially regularised
  fits, a curvature penalty on the fitted surfaces, fixed or estimated
  point-spread functions, and model-driven refinement of the periosteal
  segmentation. Rust with Python bindings (cortical_bone_mapping_rs).
authors:
  - family-names: Neeteson
    given-names: Nathan J.
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/njneeteson/cortical-bone-mapping-rs
keywords:
  - cortical bone mapping
  - cortical thickness
  - HR-pQCT
  - CT
  - bone
  - image analysis
  - Rust
  - Python
